# Stage 2 — inspect-only (real hardware, oracle STAYS RUNNING)

Date: 2026-09-25T23:38:30+01:00
Tag: v0.1.2-test3
Binary: target/release/tbard (real mode, NOT --dry-run)
Oracle: tiny-dfr-mbp142 PID 562 on /dev/dri/card0 (must stay running + lit)

## Run — tbard real mode, tight 6s timeout (capture discovery verdicts, kill before render)

The binary has no --inspect flag. discover_touchbar_drm() scans all cards
READ-ONLY (O_RDONLY, no master) and logs a verdict per card BEFORE
try_open_card attempts to acquire master on the accepted candidate.
The oracle holds card0 master, so try_open_card's acquire_master_lock
on card0 is expected to fail (EACCES) — the daemon will retry and
never reach the render loop. timeout SIGTERM ensures clean exit.

### Oracle state BEFORE
```
                     USER        PID ACCESS COMMAND
/dev/dri/card0:      nobody      562 F.... tiny-dfr-mbp142
```

